Report how much memory a surface's terminal holds.

ghostty#14499 added a terminal's memory to libghostty-vt's
ghostty_terminal_get, but the embedding API has no matching call, so an app
hosting surfaces cannot tell one tab's scrollback from its own memory. This
adds ghostty_surface_memory_usage, the resident bytes of both screens' pages
and Kitty images, read under the renderer lock as ghostty_surface_read_text
reads the screen. Asked for upstream in ghostty-org/ghostty discussion #14524.

Written for Multishell, cut as a `git diff` against the ThirdParty/ghostty pin.

